          "title": "You'll want to know: daraufhin",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "daraufhin — \"as a result, thereupon\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Der Bus kam nicht. Daraufhin nahmen wir ein Taxi. The bus did not come. As a result, we took a taxi."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It says that one thing led to the next. The verb comes second: Daraufhin rief sie an."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "daraufhin joins darauf \"on that, after that\" and hin \"towards, away\", all inherited Germanic pieces; EtymDB lists no parent for the whole, which is a modern compound."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
